{
  "case_id": "2018-18-422",
  "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear\nargument first this morning in Case 18-422,\nRucho versus Common Cause.\nMr. Clement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This Court has repeatedly failed to identify a justiciable standard for partisan gerrymandering claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Clement, that ship has sailed in Baker v. Carr. Once we decided the one-person, one-vote concept, we've been pretty much in all of our jurisprudence saying that certain acts by the legislature are unconstitutional, including race discrimination and others."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: -- Mr. Clement, does one person have one vote that counts equally, which I take it to be the -- the message of those cases, now well accepted, does one person have one vote that counts equally with others if the impact of her vote is reduced based on her party affiliation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: All right, I've got this point, but what I'm trying to get you to focus on -- because I've read the briefs, you know, I -- this is the fourth time, and I -- and I -- I think I -- but the thing that I want you to focus on, if you can, if you want to, is the two-thirds majority idea."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: On -- on proportional representation, can I ask a question, which is, first, isn't proportional representation a judicially-manageable standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF EMMET J. BONDURANT, II ON BEHALF OF THE APPELLEES, COMMON CAUSE, ET AL."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that partisanship has to be at least a material factor, as it is in Arlington Heights or Mount Healthy, but, in this case, we prove that was a predominant factor, and that is the ruling of the lower court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, counsel, that -- that first one, dictate electoral outcomes, I think is going to turn -- turn on -- on numbers, right? How much deviation from proportional representation is enough to dictate an outcome?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bondurant",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is you cannot discriminate intentionally against political parties and voters based on their political views and their voting history."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus briefs",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm given to understand by the amicus briefs in this case that nuclear plants are built based on statistical models."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The one thing about statistical models is there's always the possibility of an aberration, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, counsel, I get -- I get that, you know, you've -- you've wisely adopted a very fine answer, given for you. But I guess my question is, once we control for geography, once we control for all those things, we're going to have hundreds and hundreds of maps, as Justice Alito has pointed out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Do you agree with Mr. Clement that the Constitution does not require proportional representation or require something close to proportional representation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, if we look at the -- the popular vote for the House of Representatives nationally in the 2018 election and compare that to the percentage of seats won by the two parties, what -- to what degree do they diverge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Clement",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Thank you, Your Honors. Just a few points in two minutes. First, I do think at a very fundamental level my friends on the other side are the victim of their own technology because they have produced 24,000 maps that are"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2934b92e16c40a3aa68a880d4e654770e0013d55648203b011162480b1c75760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2934b92e16c4-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
